{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Population Simulation Ensemble — Emergent Patterns\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo runs **50 agents for 30 days** on a Watts-Strogatz small-world network. After each daily step, it extracts per-phase metrics from every agent via `_last_phase_outputs` and computes population-level aggregates for all 5 modules.\n",
        "\n",
        "The theory predicts: stress prevalence fluctuates with event generation, coping success rate is modulated by network structure (well-connected agents cope better), resource inequality emerges from differing stress histories, and affect variance decreases over time as social convergence operates.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "2489df91"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from numpy.random import Generator, PCG64\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.model import StressModel\n",
        "from src.python.demos.module_metrics import (\n",
        "    aggregate_perception,\n",
        "    aggregate_activation,\n",
        "    aggregate_allocation,\n",
        "    aggregate_buffering,\n",
        "    aggregate_daily_cycle,\n",
        "    extract_perception_metrics,\n",
        "    extract_activation_metrics,\n",
        "    extract_allocation_metrics,\n",
        "    extract_buffering_metrics,\n",
        "    extract_daily_cycle_metrics,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "_FACTORS = [\"social_support\", \"family_support\", \"formal_intervention\", \"psychological_capital\"]"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Run Loop\n",
        "\n",
        "50 agents × 30 days. Per-agent metrics extracted and aggregated each day."
      ],
      "id": "60b109d6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: run\n",
        "model = StressModel(N=50, max_days=30, seed=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "daily_aggregates = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for day in range(model.max_days):\n",
        "    model.step()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Collect per-agent metrics\n",
        "    all_perception = []\n",
        "    all_activation = []\n",
        "    all_allocation = []\n",
        "    all_buffering = []\n",
        "    all_daily = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for agent in model.agents:\n",
        "        pre_state = agent._build_agent_state()\n",
        "        last = agent._last_phase_outputs\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Extract metrics from each module\n",
        "        p_metrics = extract_perception_metrics(last.get(\"stress_perception\"), pre_state)\n",
        "        a_metrics = extract_activation_metrics(last.get(\"resilience_activation\"), pre_state)\n",
        "        alloc_metrics = extract_allocation_metrics(last.get(\"resource_allocation\"), pre_state)\n",
        "        buff_metrics = extract_buffering_metrics(last.get(\"stress_buffering\"), pre_state)\n",
        "\n",
        "        post_state = agent._build_agent_state()\n",
        "        reset_out = last.get(\"daily_reset\")\n",
        "        affect_out = last.get(\"affect_dynamics\")\n",
        "        pss10_out = last.get(\"pss10_consolidation\")\n",
        "        d_metrics = extract_daily_cycle_metrics(pre_state, post_state, reset_out, affect_out, pss10_out)\n",
        "\n",
        "        if p_metrics: all_perception.append(p_metrics)\n",
        "        if a_metrics: all_activation.append(a_metrics)\n",
        "        if alloc_metrics: all_allocation.append(alloc_metrics)\n",
        "        if buff_metrics: all_buffering.append(buff_metrics)\n",
        "        if d_metrics: all_daily.append(d_metrics)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Aggregate\n",
        "    daily_aggregates.append({\n",
        "        \"day\": day,\n",
        "        \"perception\": aggregate_perception(all_perception),\n",
        "        \"activation\": aggregate_activation(all_activation),\n",
        "        \"allocation\": aggregate_allocation(all_allocation),\n",
        "        \"buffering\": aggregate_buffering(all_buffering),\n",
        "        \"daily\": aggregate_daily_cycle(all_daily),\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "df_agg = pd.DataFrame([\n",
        "    {\"day\": d[\"day\"],\n",
        "     \"stress_prevalence\": d[\"perception\"].get(\"stress_prevalence\", 0),\n",
        "     \"coping_success_rate\": d[\"activation\"].get(\"coping_success_rate\", 0),\n",
        "     \"avg_regeneration\": d[\"allocation\"].get(\"regeneration_mean\", 0),\n",
        "     \"avg_buffering_strength\": d[\"buffering\"].get(\"buffering_strength_mean\", 0),\n",
        "     \"avg_affect_reset\": d[\"daily\"].get(\"affect_reset_magnitude_mean\", 0),\n",
        "     \"avg_stress_decay\": d[\"daily\"].get(\"stress_decay_mean\", 0),\n",
        "     \"avg_pss10\": d[\"daily\"].get(\"pss10_mean\", 15),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    for d in daily_aggregates\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Population ensemble: {len(df_agg)} days, {len(model.agents)} agents\")"
      ],
      "id": "run",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 1 — Population Perception: Stress Prevalence"
      ],
      "id": "b4fc0350"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-pop-perception\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df_agg[\"day\"], df_agg[\"stress_prevalence\"], \"r-\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Proportion Stressed\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Stress Prevalence Over Time\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_ylim(0, 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# PSS-10 trend\n",
        "pss10_by_day = {d[\"day\"]: [] for d in daily_aggregates}\n",
        "for d in daily_aggregates:\n",
        "    pss10_by_day[d[\"day\"]] = [d[\"daily\"].get(\"pss10_mean\", 15)]\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].plot(df_agg[\"day\"], df_agg[\"avg_pss10\"], \"purple\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Mean PSS-10\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Mean PSS-10 Over Time\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-pop-perception",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 2 — Population Activation: Coping Success Rate"
      ],
      "id": "157abd9e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-pop-activation\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df_agg[\"day\"], df_agg[\"coping_success_rate\"], \"g-\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "axes[0].axhline(y=0.5, color=\"grey\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Coping Success Rate\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Population Coping Success Rate\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_ylim(0, 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Coping success rate distribution across agents\n",
        "coping_rates = []\n",
        "for agent in model.agents:\n",
        "    events = getattr(agent, \"last_daily_stress_events\", [])\n",
        "    if events:\n",
        "        successes = sum(1 for e in events if e.get(\"coped_successfully\", False))\n",
        "        coping_rates.append(successes / len(events))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].hist(coping_rates, bins=15, color=\"#2ecc71\", alpha=0.7)\n",
        "axes[1].axvline(x=np.mean(coping_rates), color=\"red\", linestyle=\"--\", label=f\"mean={np.mean(coping_rates):.2f}\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Agent Coping Success Rate\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Coping Rate Distribution Across Agents\")\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-pop-activation",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 3 — Population Allocation: Resource Dynamics"
      ],
      "id": "6f48a83c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-pop-allocation\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df_agg[\"day\"], df_agg[\"avg_regeneration\"], \"orange\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Mean Regeneration\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Average Resource Regeneration\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Agent-level resource distribution (final day)\n",
        "final_resources = [agent.resources for agent in model.agents]\n",
        "axes[1].hist(final_resources, bins=20, color=\"orange\", alpha=0.7)\n",
        "axes[1].axvline(x=np.mean(final_resources), color=\"red\", linestyle=\"--\",\n",
        "                label=f\"mean={np.mean(final_resources):.2f}\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Resources (final day)\");\n",
        "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Final Resource Distribution\")\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-pop-allocation",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 4 — Population Buffering: Stress Mitigation"
      ],
      "id": "81c773a0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-pop-buffering\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df_agg[\"day\"], df_agg[\"avg_buffering_strength\"], \"g-\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Mean Buffering Strength\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Average Buffering Strength Over Time\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Buffering vs coping success\n",
        "final_buffering = []\n",
        "final_coping = []\n",
        "for agent in model.agents:\n",
        "    last = agent._last_phase_outputs\n",
        "    buff_out = last.get(\"stress_buffering\")\n",
        "    if buff_out:\n",
        "        final_buffering.append(buff_out[\"observation\"].get(\"buffering_strength\", 0))\n",
        "        events = getattr(agent, \"last_daily_stress_events\", [])\n",
        "        success_rate = sum(1 for e in events if e.get(\"coped_successfully\", False)) / max(len(events), 1)\n",
        "        final_coping.append(success_rate)\n",
        "\n",
        "if final_buffering:\n",
        "    axes[1].scatter(final_buffering, final_coping, alpha=0.6)\n",
        "    axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Buffering Strength\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Coping Success Rate\")\n",
        "    axes[1].set_title(\"Buffering vs Coping (Final Day)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-pop-buffering",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 5 — Population Daily Cycle: Reset & PSS-10"
      ],
      "id": "da08aa71"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-pop-daily\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df_agg[\"day\"], df_agg[\"avg_affect_reset\"], \"b-\", linewidth=2, label=\"affect reset\")\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df_agg[\"day\"], df_agg[\"avg_stress_decay\"], \"r-\", linewidth=2, label=\"stress decay\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Mean Amount\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Daily Reset & Decay Over Time\")\n",
        "axes[0].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Final PSS-10 distribution\n",
        "final_pss10 = [agent.pss10 for agent in model.agents]\n",
        "axes[1].hist(final_pss10, bins=20, color=\"purple\", alpha=0.7)\n",
        "axes[1].axvline(x=np.mean(final_pss10), color=\"red\", linestyle=\"--\",\n",
        "                label=f\"mean={np.mean(final_pss10):.1f}\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"PSS-10 Score\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Final PSS-10 Distribution\")\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-pop-daily",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Network Effects"
      ],
      "id": "8d0f99c2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-network\n",
        "from src.python.math_utils import create_rng\n",
        "\n",
        "# Check if network coordinates are available\n",
        "pos = getattr(model.grid, \"pos\", None)\n",
        "if pos is None:\n",
        "    # Generate simple circular layout\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        pos = nx.circular_layout(model.grid.G)\n",
        "    except Exception:\n",
        "        pos = None\n",
        "\n",
        "if pos:\n",
        "    resilience_vals = [agent.resilience for agent in model.agents]\n",
        "    node_colors = [agent.resilience for agent in model.agents]\n",
        "\n",
        "    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
        "    nx.draw(model.grid.G, pos, node_color=node_colors, cmap=\"RdYlGn\",\n",
        "            node_size=80, edge_color=\"grey\", alpha=0.7, ax=ax)\n",
        "    sm = plt.cm.ScalarMappable(cmap=\"RdYlGn\")\n",
        "    sm.set_array(resilience_vals)\n",
        "    plt.colorbar(sm, ax=ax, label=\"Resilience\")\n",
        "    ax.set_title(\"Agent Network Colored by Final Resilience\")\n",
        "    plt.show()\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"Network layout not available; skipping network visualization\")"
      ],
      "id": "fig-network",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What We See\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Stress prevalence** fluctuates but stays bounded: daily reset prevents indefinite accumulation.\n",
        "- **Coping success rate** varies across the population, driven by individual differences in resilience and social network position.\n",
        "- **Resource dynamics** show convergence over time: regeneration is higher when resources are low.\n",
        "- **Buffering strength** tracks population resource levels, confirming the mediation pathway.\n",
        "- **PSS-10 distribution** shows individual differences driven by stress exposure and coping capacity.\n",
        "- **Network effects**: agents with higher centrality (more connections) tend to have higher resilience due to more support exchanges.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why This Matters\n",
        "\n",
        "Population-level patterns emerge from individual-level mechanisms. The module-by-module breakdown at the population scale reveals which mechanisms drive the overall stress dynamics. This is essential for designing interventions: if stress prevalence is driven by poor buffering, strengthen the resources pathway; if driven by high event frequency, reduce exposure."
      ],
      "id": "ee696c9a"
    }
  ],
